description:
pkix-path/src/lib.rs:1657

Clippy pedantic flags 'this could be rewritten as let...else':

  let domain = match subject.split_once('@') {
      Some((_, d)) => d,
      None => return false, // malformed subject
  };

The idiomatic form since Rust 1.65 is:

  let Some((_, domain)) = subject.split_once('@') else {
      return false; // malformed subject
  };

MSRV is 1.73, so let-else is available. The let-else form is cleaner and reduces one level of nesting.
